CASE({
  id: 'tamponade', cat: ['CVS', 'Resp'], covers: ['Pericardial effusion / cardiac tamponade (obstructive shock)'], title: 'Breathless with a quiet heart', dx: 'Cardiac tamponade from a large (tuberculous) pericardial effusion',
  syn: ['tamponade', 'pericardial effusion', 'tb pericarditis'], dxKw: ['tamponade|pericardial effusion', 'beck|pulsus|muffled|jvp', 'tb|tubercul|cause'],
  dxWhy: 'Breathlessness, hypotension, raised JVP and muffled heart sounds (Beck\'s triad) with pulsus paradoxus, a globular heart on CXR and low-voltage ECG with electrical alternans = cardiac tamponade (obstructive shock). In SA with HIV, TB pericarditis is the commonest cause.',
  susp: 'Obstructive shock — cardiac tamponade from a pericardial effusion (TB pericarditis is common in SA, especially with HIV); differentials heart failure, PE, constrictive pericarditis.',
  suspKw: ['tamponade|pericardial', 'tb|tubercul', 'heart failure|pe|constrict|obstruct'],
  avoid: ['hiv', 'hf'],
  gen: r => {
    const sex = r.sex(0.5), age = r.int(24, 46);
    return {
      sex, age, build: r.build({cachectic: 2, thin: 2, normal: 1}), setting: r.hosp(), job: r.pick(['miner', 'cleaner', 'unemployed', 'street vendor']),
      brief: `${r.int(3, 6)} weeks of night sweats, weight loss, worsening breathlessness; now dizzy and faint on standing. HIV+, CD4 unknown.`, pc: '"I can\'t breathe properly and when I stand up everything goes dark."',
      v: {hr: r.int(118, 132), sbp: r.int(82, 94), dbp: r.int(64, 72), rr: 28, sat: 94, t: 37.8, gcs: 15},
      signs: ['breathless', 'jvp', 'sweaty', 'cachectic'], flags: {hiv: true, cardiogenic: true, untreatedTB: true},
      ecg: {lowVolt: true, alternans: true, rate: 124},
      lab: {CD4: [80, 260], VL: [10000, 200000], Hb: [9.4, 11], CRP: [60, 120], ESR: [70, 110]},
      prof: [[`${age} years old`, 0, '—'], ['HIV positive, defaulted ART', 1, 'HIV → TB → TB pericarditis is the leading cause of pericardial effusion in SA.'], ['Night sweats and weight loss', 1, 'Constitutional TB symptoms.'], ['Former gold miner', 1, 'Silica exposure ↑ TB risk.'], ['Supports Orlando Pirates', 0, '—']],
      hx: [['Breathlessness', 'Getting worse for weeks. Now even talking makes me tired.', 1], ['Chest discomfort', 'A heavy dull feeling in the chest; better leaning forward.', 1], ['Dizziness', 'Faint when I stand.', 1], ['Constitutional', 'Night sweats, lost a lot of weight, fevers.', 1], ['HIV / ART', 'Positive since 2018, stopped ART last year.', 1], ['TB contacts', 'My cousin in the same room had TB.', 1]],
      ex: [['Cardiovascular', 'Tachycardic, BP 88/68 (narrow pulse pressure), pulsus paradoxus 18 mmHg (pulse fades on inspiration), JVP raised with Kussmaul sign, apex impalpable, heart sounds muffled/distant.', 1], ['Respiratory', 'Dullness at the left infrascapular region (Ewart\'s sign). Otherwise clear.', 1], ['Abdomen', 'Tender hepatomegaly, mild ascites.', 0]],
      res: {ECHO: 'Large circumferential pericardial effusion (2.6 cm) with fibrinous strands; RA and RV diastolic collapse; IVC plethoric — echocardiographic tamponade.', PLEU: 'Pericardiocentesis fluid: exudate, lymphocyte-predominant, ADA raised; Xpert MTB/RIF Ultra: MTB detected, rifampicin resistance not detected.', SPXP: 'MTB detected (trace).', HIVR: 'Reactive.'},
      cxr: {globular: true, ctr: 0.72},
    };
  },
  keyInv: ['ECHO', 'ECG', 'CXR'], okInv: ['PANEL_FBC', 'PANEL_UE', 'HIVR', 'PANEL_CD4', 'SPXP', 'PLEU', 'PANEL_ESR', 'PANEL_CRP'],
  must: [{k: 'proc_pericard', n: 'Urgent pericardiocentesis', why: 'Relieves the obstruction to ventricular filling — definitive emergency treatment.'}, {k: 'antitb', n: 'Anti-TB treatment (RHZE) once confirmed', why: 'TB pericarditis is the likely cause; ART 2 weeks after TB treatment starts (watch IRIS).'}],
  good: {proc_pericard: {m: 'Pericardiocentesis: 600 ml straw-coloured fluid drained — BP rising, pulsus paradoxus gone.', fx: {v: {sbp: +32, hr: -28, rr: -8}, unsign: ['jvp']}}, ivfluid_bolus: {m: 'Small fluid bolus temporarily supports preload (the RV needs filling pressure).', fx: {v: {sbp: +6}}}},
  bad: {loop: {sev: 'harm', t: 'Diuretic in tamponade', m: 'Tamponade is preload-dependent — the heart can only fill against the effusion by high venous pressure. Diuresis drops preload → cardiac output collapses.', fx: {v: {sbp: -18, hr: +10}}}, nitrate: {sev: 'harm', t: 'Venodilator in tamponade', m: 'Reducing preload in tamponade drops CO further.', fx: {v: {sbp: -20}}}},
  crit: {after: 30, every: 10, fx: {sbp: -5, hr: +4}, stop: ['proc_pericard'], msg: 'Tamponade progressed to PEA-type collapse — urgent pericardiocentesis was needed.'},
  Q: [
    {s: 'mech', q: 'Explain how fluid in the pericardium causes shock and pulsus paradoxus.', a: 'Fluid accumulating in the non-distensible pericardium raises intrapericardial pressure → compresses the chambers (RA/RV diastolic collapse) → impaired diastolic filling → ↓ stroke volume and CO = obstructive shock ("pipes blocked"), with raised venous pressure. On inspiration, venous return to the right heart increases; with a fixed total pericardial volume the septum bulges into the LV (ventricular interdependence) → LV filling and SV fall → systolic BP drops > 10 mmHg = pulsus paradoxus.', kw: ['pericardi|pressure', 'filling|diastol', 'obstruct|cardiac output|stroke volume', 'inspiration|septum|interdepend', 'pulsus']},
    {s: 'cause', q: 'What causes pericardial effusions?', a: 'Inflammation from infection or immunological causes (as in pericarditis — TB is commonest in SA, esp. with HIV; viral, bacterial; SLE, uraemia, post-MI/Dressler\'s), trauma causing bleeding into the pericardial space, non-infectious conditions altering Starling forces (heart failure, hypoalbuminaemia), malignancy, and decreased drainage of pericardial fluid.', kw: ['tb|tubercul', 'infect|viral|inflamm', 'trauma|bleed', 'starling|heart failure|albumin|malignan|uraemi']},
    {s: 'inv', q: 'What are the clinical and investigation hallmarks of tamponade?', a: 'Beck\'s triad: hypotension, muffled heart sounds, raised JVP; pulsus paradoxus; Kussmaul sign; Ewart\'s sign (dullness/bronchial breathing below the left scapula from lung compression). ECG: low voltage, electrical alternans, tachycardia. CXR: globular "water-bottle" heart with clear lungs. Echo: effusion with RA/RV diastolic collapse (diagnostic). Fluid analysis: exudate, lymphocytes, ADA, Xpert for TB.', kw: ['beck', 'hypotens', 'muffled|distant', 'jvp', 'pulsus', 'low voltage|alternans', 'globular|water bottle', 'echo']},
    {s: 'mgmt', q: 'How is this patient treated?', a: 'Emergency pericardiocentesis (echo-guided) — the definitive treatment of tamponade; support preload (avoid diuretics/venodilators; small fluid bolus); O₂; send fluid for chemistry, cell count, ADA, Gram stain, Xpert/culture, cytology. Treat the cause: anti-TB therapy (RHZE), start ART 2 weeks after TB treatment (watch for IRIS), co-trimoxazole prophylaxis; monitor for constrictive pericarditis.', kw: ['pericardiocentesis|drain', 'avoid diuretic|preload|fluid', 'rhze|anti-tb|tb treatment', 'art|antiretroviral|iris']},
  ],
  summary: 'Obstructive shock: effusion ↑ pericardial pressure → impaired diastolic filling. Causes: TB (commonest in SA/HIV), viral, bacterial, uraemia, SLE, malignancy, trauma, Dressler\'s, Starling-force changes. Beck\'s triad (hypotension, muffled heart sounds, ↑ JVP), pulsus paradoxus, Kussmaul, Ewart\'s sign. ECG low voltage + electrical alternans; CXR globular heart; echo diastolic collapse. Rx: pericardiocentesis, keep preload (no diuretics/nitrates), treat cause (RHZE; ART after 2 weeks).',
  src: 'Illness scripts (pericardial effusions, Beck\'s triad); IEYA shock pages', real: [],
});
